# Generated media (audio/video) — Week 3's media/video-generation layers
# write real files here (studio/data/media-tmp/, studio/data/videos/); never
# committed, same reasoning as node_modules/dist. `**/data/*` (not bare
# `data/`, not `data/*`) deliberately: a bare `data/` has no "middle" slash
# so it matches at any depth (studio/data/) but fully excludes the
# directory, stopping git from descending into it to evaluate the
# audio-beds negation below; a plain `data/*` (a middle slash) is anchored
# to the repo root, only matching a root-level data/ that doesn't exist
# here at all (the real one is studio/data/). `**/data/*` matches at any
# depth *and* only excludes direct children, leaving `data/` itself
# traversable so the negation below actually applies.
**/data/*
# Sprint 2 Task 3 exception: data/audio-beds/ is a small, curated, checked-in
# royalty-free music library (studio/src/audio-bed/manifest.ts), not
# runtime-generated scratch — the one deliberate carve-out from the blanket
# data/ ignore above.
!**/data/audio-beds/
# Sprint 4 Task 8 (R2) exception: data/fonts/ holds the bundled, OFL-licensed caption
# font (+ its licence) so laptop and VPS render captions identically.
!**/data/fonts/
# Sprint 6 Task 2 (P5): the one pre-rendered disclaimer clip and its manifest (platform asset, checked in).
!**/data/disclaimer/

.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
Claude outputs
